    <comment>New package: LiveKit's WebRTC (M137, commit 0001d84) built from source as a shared library. zed's calls feature needs it (webrtc-sys). Without it, zed's build would download livekit's prebuilt libwebrtc.a, which OBS cannot do.

- Source0 is maintainer-generated from a gclient checkout. make-source.sh (Source1) reproduces it.
- It builds against the system dav1d, ffmpeg, libaom, libjpeg-turbo, libvpx, openh264, opus and zlib. The rest stays bundled and is declared with Provides: bundled(). BoringSSL is symbol-prefixed so it cannot clash with the system OpenSSL.
- SONAME libwebrtc-suse.so.137 is ours, not upstream's. It is bumped with every snapshot because each snapshot is a new ABI.
- Disabled on 16.0: libaom's SVE code needs GCC 14 or newer.
- README.SUSE-maint documents the bump procedure and the lockstep with zed.

Submitted before zed, which build-requires it.</comment>
    <requestid>1379959</requestid>
